# Next.js Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define App Router structure, layouts, and route conventions
- Enforce Server Components by default
- Standardize loading, error, and not-found UI patterns
- Configure metadata, SEO, and route handlers

## Best Practices

- Use route groups `(auth)`, `(dashboard)` for layout organization without URL segments
- Colocate `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx` with routes
- Use `generateMetadata` for dynamic page titles
- Parallel routes only when genuinely needed (e.g., modals)
- Route Handlers (`app/api/`) only for webhooks, file uploads, third-party callbacks
- Prefer Server Actions over API routes for internal mutations

## Coding Standards

- Page files export default async Server Components
- Extract interactive parts to Client Components in same feature folder
- Use `redirect()` and `notFound()` from `next/navigation` in Server Components
- Dynamic segments: `[id]`, catch-all `[...slug]` with validation
- Environment variables: `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix only for client-safe values

## Folder Structure

```
src/app/
├── (auth)/
│   ├── login/page.tsx
│   ├── register/page.tsx
│   └── layout.tsx
├── (dashboard)/
│   ├── layout.tsx              # Sidebar + header shell
│   ├── page.tsx                # Dashboard home
│   ├── cases/
│   │   ├── page.tsx
│   │   ├── loading.tsx
│   │   ├── [caseId]/
│   │   │   ├── page.tsx
│   │   │   └── edit/page.tsx
│   │   └── new/page.tsx
│   ├── clients/
│   ├── calendar/
│   ├── billing/
│   └── settings/
├── api/
│   └── webhooks/
│       └── stripe/route.ts
├── layout.tsx                  # Root layout (providers, fonts)
├── globals.css
├── not-found.tsx
└── error.tsx
```

## Naming Convention

| File | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Page | `page.tsx` |
| Layout | `layout.tsx` |
| Loading | `loading.tsx` |
| Error | `error.tsx` (must be Client Component) |
| Route handler | `route.ts` |
| Route segment folder | kebab-case plural | `cases/`, `hearings/` |

## Performance Rules

- Static generation where data is public and stable
- `revalidatePath` / `revalidateTag` after mutations
- Use `Suspense` boundaries with skeleton fallbacks
- Dynamic imports for heavy client components: `next/dynamic`
- Image optimization via `next/image` always

## Security Rules

- Middleware auth check on all `(dashboard)` routes
- Never pass secrets to Client Components
- CSRF protection via Server Actions (built-in)
- Validate route params before DB queries

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Async Server Component page
// app/(dashboard)/cases/[caseId]/page.tsx
import { CaseDetailView } from '@/features/cases/ui/case-detail-view';
import { caseRepository } from '@/repositories/case.repository';
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

interface Props { params: Promise<{ caseId: string }> }

export default async function CaseDetailPage({ params }: Props) {
  const { caseId } = await params;
  const caseData = await caseRepository.findById(caseId);
  if (!caseData) notFound();
  return <CaseDetailView case={caseData} />;
}

// ❌ BAD — fetch in Client Component when Server Component suffices
'use client';
export default function Page() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/cases').then(...) }, []);
}
```

## Things to Avoid

- `getServerSideProps` / Pages Router patterns
- API routes for CRUD that Server Actions handle
- Passing large objects as props to Client Components
- Missing loading states on async routes
- Hardcoded URLs — use centralized route constants in `lib/routes.ts`

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Page is Server Component unless interactivity required
- [ ] `loading.tsx` skeleton exists for data-heavy routes
- [ ] Route params validated before use
- [ ] Metadata set (title, description)
- [ ] Mutations use Server Actions, not client fetch to API
- [ ] Revalidation triggered after data changes
